# Bulk ship (git / PR)

Do **not** push or open a PR after every edit. That is noisy.

## Default while working

1. One branch per **topic** (or one session branch): `docs/…`, `fix/…`, `feature/…`, `build/…`. Never commit on `main`.
2. Edit and **commit locally** as needed.
3. **No `git push`.** **No PR URL.** **No `gh pr create`.**

## When the user ships

| User says | Agent does |
| --- | --- |
| **`push`** | `git push -u origin HEAD` only. Report the remote branch. Do not open a PR unless they also asked. |
| **`PR`** / **`ship`** / **`bulk ship`** | Push if needed, then open **one** PR for all commits on this branch since `main` (prefer `gh pr create` when `gh` is on PATH and authenticated; otherwise the GitHub “Compare & pull request” / `pull/new/<branch>` link). Return the PR URL. |

`bulk ship` means the same as `ship`: one push + one PR covering the whole branch, not one PR per commit.

## Commit messages, PR titles and PR bodies

Say what changed and why, in plain words, so a reviewer understands it without opening `doc/`. Start the PR title with the branch type (`docs:`, `build:`, `feature:`, `fix:`).

- Never use the user's shortcut words in them: `mosaic`, `mosaic done`, `push`, `ship`, `PR`, `merge`, `go`, `replan`. They are instructions to the agent, not history.
- Never use internal labels that need the docs to decode: `milestone 14`, `PR 2`, `step E`. Describe the thing itself (for example "address screen and sign-in", not "step E").
- Do not mention that other PRs were merged; the PR list already shows that. Do not add a "not changed" list or a test plan the change does not need.
- Fix a bad title or body with `gh pr edit`. Reword an unmerged commit with `git commit --amend` plus `git push --force-with-lease` on the topic branch only, never on `main`.

## Status edits on `ship`

When the user says `ship` / `PR` / `bulk ship` for a topic branch that changed behaviour, update the status docs **before** pushing and commit them on the same branch, so the PR carries them and no docs-only PR follows the merge: `doc/status.md` and `.cursor/rules/mosaicwave-status.mdc` (Next paragraph, same date), the ticked items in `doc/progress-todo.md`, and a dated row in `doc/progress-archive.md`. This never marks a milestone done; that stays `milestone N done` only.

## Status edits (`mosaic done`, `milestone N done`)

Wrap-up and milestone-done edits (status, the status rule, progress, archive, roadmap) must not each get their own PR.

1. **Reuse an unmerged branch.** If the current topic branch is not merged yet (local only, or its PR is open), commit the status edits there. Check with `gh pr list --head <branch> --state all` before branching.
2. **Only when every branch is merged**, create one `docs/status-<topic>` branch from the latest `main`. Any later `mosaic done` or `milestone N done` reuses it until it merges.
3. **Open PR:** commit on its branch; on `ship`, push to update that PR. Do not open a second one.
4. **Wrap-up right before a milestone gate:** if the wrap-up reports that only `milestone N done` is left, say in the report that shipping after `milestone N done` puts both in one PR.

## Do not

- Create a new branch for every tiny follow-up on the same topic — keep committing on the open topic branch.
- Squash-merge or delete remote branches unless the user asks.
- Treat **`go`** (plan approval) as permission to push or open a PR.
